## Why This Is Asked
Assesses on-device streaming ASR design with privacy, domain adaptation, and real-time constraints. 

## Key Concepts
- Streaming encoder-decoder models, CTC decoding, lexicon and LM integration
- On-device quantization and energy profiling
- Federated updates with secure aggregation and privacy guarantees
- Drift detection via per-user and per-domain metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
function streamDecode(chunk, state) {
  const features = extractFeatures(chunk);
  const logits = model.encodeDecode(features, state);
  const text = decodeCTC(logits);
  return text;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency under varying network/CPU loads? 
- How would you roll out vocabulary updates without sacrificing privacy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design for real-time fraud scoring at scale with privacy constraints, multi-tenant data sharing, and safe rollbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming feature store and time-window features
- Hybrid inference paths: server-side and on-device
- Federated learning with differential privacy
- Drift detection and canary-based rollout strategies
- Model calibration and per-transaction explainability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo scoring sketch
function score(tx, globalModel, localModel){
  const feats = extract(tx)
  const s1 = globalModel.predict(feats)
  const s2 = localModel.predict(feats)
  return calibrate((0.6*s1 + 0.4*s2));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle label latency for online updates?
- What metrics trigger rollback and how would you test rollbacks?

